      "writtenOn": "2025-09-09T08:51:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I\u0027m not a huge fan of that init_lock myself.  It literally just says \"don\u0027t reset the device and its data, because I\u0027m currently using it\". It probably can become some smart ref-counter or something of that nature.\n\nSwitching recompression/writeback knobs to a writer init_lock will basically block other zram device attrs for the duration of post-processing, e.g. mm_stat monitoring etc.  Which *maybe* isn\u0027t the end of the world, but a little difficult to reason about.",
      "parentUuid": "b8359652_cbb3f286",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 166,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 166,
        "endChar": 16
      },
